      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The divisor-sum, prime-cutoff, and Farey criteria each normalize or center a dominant term so that the remaining proof burden lies in a one-sided secondary comparison. Exact substitutions, bounded coordinate changes, and finite-versus-tail partitions preserve only their stated inequalities or asymptotic scales; complementary limits without rate or side control do not.",
