      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_48dfde6463f630cfefc1fdca3d77e614415e94574cf49ccfdbbce97778053923",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Completion provides a shared s↦1−s reflection form while retaining family-specific factors; the Eisenstein example additionally separates reflection in s from modular invariance in z, and the Davenport–Heilbronn example shows that functional-equation symmetry can coexist with off-critical-line zeros. Reflection is therefore structural infrastructure, not a zero-line criterion.",
