      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4e066504aeffe402ad77fc326bcbdc1175eaa3c996d79ba0a481c5da7db7d12c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Random-matrix comparisons become meaningful only after representation changes suited to distributions. Unfolding removes height-dependent mean density from zero spacings, while shifted Jensen polynomials approach fixed-degree Hermite normal forms in a separate derivative limit and Hermite degree growth supplies a GUE-compatible root law. Neither bridge certifies the horizontal location of zeta zeros.",
